## Implementation Finalization Checklist

- [ ] All requirements implemented and verified
- [ ] Code quality standards met (linting, formatting, type checking)
- [ ] Performance optimizations applied
- [ ] Comprehensive test coverage achieved
- [ ] Accessibility standards met
- [ ] Documentation completed
- [ ] Bundle size optimized
- [ ] No remaining TODOs or FIXMEs
- [ ] Final verification completed successfully

## Best Practices

1. **Incremental Finalization**: Finalize incrementally rather than all at once
2. **Metrics-Driven**: Use objective metrics to determine readiness
3. **User-Centric**: Prioritize user-facing improvements
4. **Performance-First**: Treat performance as a core requirement
5. **Complete Testing**: Ensure comprehensive test coverage before finalization

## Common Finalization Issues

| Issue | Solution | Implementation |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| Large bundle size | Code splitting, tree shaking | Split routes, use dynamic imports |
| Type errors | Proper type definitions | Define interfaces, use proper types |
| Accessibility violations | ARIA attributes, semantic HTML | Use correct roles, labels, and semantic elements |
| Low test coverage | Add missing tests | Focus on critical paths and edge cases |
| Performance bottlenecks | Component optimization | Use memo, useCallback, useMemo |

